From: Nuxel Project <nuxel@nuxel.org>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] HOST: fix file2alias.c uuid_t clash on Darwin

On macOS (Darwin) the system <sys/_types/_uuid_t.h>, pulled in through
<ctype.h>/<stdbool.h>/<stdint.h>, already defines `uuid_t` as a typedef
for `__darwin_uuid_t` (= unsigned char[16]).  scripts/mod/file2alias.c
unconditionally re-defines its own host-side `uuid_t` as a struct, which
is a redefinition error, and `struct tee_client_device_id.uuid` (declared
in include/linux/mod_devicetable.h) then refers to the Apple array type,
breaking `uuid->b[...]`.

Fix by renaming the kernel host-side type to `nuxel_host_uuid_t` through a
preprocessor alias introduced *after* the Apple system headers and
*before* the kernel mod_devicetable.h include.  The rename therefore only
affects the host tool's own typedef plus the kernel struct field in
mod_devicetable.h, and never disturbs Apple's public `uuid_t`.

Only applied by kernel/build-kernel.sh on Darwin hosts.

Signed-off-by: Nuxel Project <nuxel@nuxel.org>
---
diff --git a/scripts/mod/file2alias.c b/scripts/mod/file2alias.c
index 721e0e9f1..93253f2eb 100644
--- a/scripts/mod/file2alias.c
+++ b/scripts/mod/file2alias.c
@@ -40,6 +40,17 @@ typedef struct {
 	__u8 b[16];
 } guid_t;
 
+/*
+ * macOS/Darwin host fix (briq-k1): the Apple system libc (pulled in by
+ * <ctype.h>/<stdbool.h>/<stdint.h> above) already defines `uuid_t` as a
+ * typedef for `__darwin_uuid_t` (unsigned char[16]).  Defining our own
+ * `uuid_t` struct here is therefore a redefinition error and, worse, makes
+ * `struct tee_client_device_id.uuid` resolve to the Apple array type,
+ * breaking `uuid->b[...]`.  Alias the kernel host-side type to a unique
+ * name that cannot collide with any system header.
+ */
+#define uuid_t nuxel_host_uuid_t
+
 typedef struct {
 	__u8 b[16];
 } uuid_t;
